    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-137596",
      "publishedDate": "2026-11-26T22:55:22.010Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-11-26T22:55:22.010Z",
      "description": "A server-side request forgery (SSRF) flaw was found in KubeVirt's decentralized live migration. The connectURL field of a VirtualMachineInstanceMigration object is not validated at admission, and the privileged synchronization-controller dials the attacker-specified URL. Connection and DNS errors from the dial are exposed in a condition readable in the tenant's namespace. A user with the kubevirt.io:migrate role (a role designed for tenant delegation) can use this behavior as a blind network-reconnaissance oracle to determine the existence and connectivity of internal hosts and ports from the controller's network vantage, including services isolated from the tenant by network policy. TLS certificate pinning prevents session completion with non-KubeVirt hosts, limiting the impact to information disclosure of internal network topology; no data content, integrity, or availability impact is possible.",
      "severity": 5,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Red Hat Red Hat OpenShift Virtualization 4\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
